                <pb facs="0448" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg426"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Secretary of State Dean G. Acheson handed to Greek Ambassador in the United
                    States Athanase G. Politis in New York on October 3 a <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >note verbale</hi> of that date extending to Greece a North Atlantic Council
                    (NAC) invitation to participate in North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO)
                    planning on the defense of the Mediterranean area (Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 16, page 633). A similar
                    invitation had been conveyed to Turkey on September 19 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, page 632), which was accepted on October 2 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, page 633). Greek Ambassador Politis
                    delivered to the Department of State on October 5 a <hi rendition="#italic">note
                        verbale</hi> dated October 4 by which Greece also accepted the NAC
                    invitation (<hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>.). (For documentation on the
                    question of the relationship of Greece and Turkey to NATO, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1950v03/pg_1">volume <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>,
                        pages 1</ref> ff. and <ref target="frus:frus1950v03/pg_1108">1108</ref>
                    ff.)</p>
            </div>
